-- title:
--   Frobenius–Verschiebung datum along the reduced Frobenius lift
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $r$ and a natural number $N$ with $r \nmid N$. Let $\mathcal O$ be a commutative ring, $\pi \in \mathcal O$ with $(r) = (\pi)$ in $\mathcal O$, and let $O^{\mathrm{nr}}$ be an $\mathcal O$-algebra carrying an $\mathcal O$-algebra automorphism $\mathrm{Fr}$, such that the ideal generated by the image of $\pi$ is maximal, every monic polynomial over $O^{\mathrm{nr}}$ of positive degree has a root modulo that ideal, and $\mathrm{Fr}(x) \equiv x^r$ modulo it for all $x$. Write $k_0 = O^{\mathrm{nr}}/(\pi)$. Let $\Lambda$ be a $\mathbb Z$-submodule of $\mathbb H[\mathbb Q, a, b]$ and $A_0$ a `FakeEllipticCurve` for $\Lambda$, level $N$, over $k_0$. The assertion is the existence of a further such object $A_{0}^{(r)}$ over $k_0$ together with $\mathrm{pr} : A_0^{(r)} \to A_0$ making the square with the structure morphisms and $\operatorname{Spec}$ of `Rigidification.residueLeg π Fr` (the ring endomorphism of $k_0$ induced by $\mathrm{Fr}$) a pullback, compatibly with the relative group laws on $T$-points, with the $\Lambda$-actions, and carrying points factoring through the level morphism `lev` of $A_0^{(r)}$ to points factoring through that of $A_0$; and of morphisms $F : A_0 \to A_0^{(r)}$ and $V : A_0^{(r)} \to A_0$ over $k_0$ which are homomorphisms for the relative group laws on $T$-points, commute with the $\Lambda$-actions, preserve the property of factoring through `lev`, satisfy $V \circ F = [r]$ on $A_0$-points and $F \circ V = [r]$ on $A_0^{(r)}$-points (with $[r]$ the $r$-fold iterate `nsmulPt` of the group law), and such that $F$ is the relative Frobenius: for every commutative ring $C$ of characteristic $r$ and every $x : \operatorname{Spec} C \to A_0$, the composite $x$ followed by $F$ followed by $\mathrm{pr}$ equals $\operatorname{Spec}$ of the $r$-th power map on $C$ followed by $x$.
--
--   This is the Frobenius–Verschiebung datum for a fake elliptic curve over the residue field of an unramified base, re-addressed along the reduction of the given Frobenius lift rather than along the absolute Frobenius of $k_0$; that is the form in which rigidifications are transported when the base point is twisted. It is used in the construction of rigidifications with Frobenius-twisted data in the Čerednik–Drinfel'd comparison.
